Job Description
The China Economist is to provide basic economic research work, including to trace economic growth performance and change in policy, to manage data banks, to provide basic modeling forecast, and to response to sales/client requests for basic information
Tracking statistics of economic growth performance;
Making preliminary analysist into economic statistics;
Managing macroeconomic data banks;
Tracking changes in economic policy measures, in particular fiscal, monetary and other financial policy, etc.;
Modelling forecast for major economic indicators;
Market charts and tables for reports and presentation packages;
Meeting sales and client requests for basic information.
Participating in market call formulation;
Make charts and tables for published reports, including flush, focus, deep dive, global outlook, and other thematic reports;
Contribution to roadshow marketing materials;
Contributing to services to clients
Publication of research reports in Chinese (when management decides it to go)
Job Requirement
Master Degree or above
3-5 years related working experience will be preferred.
Research-oriented personality
Strong decision making and analytical skills
Good bilanguage of Chinese and English in speaking and writing
Takes initiative and is results driven
Act with integrity
Ability to manage change and complexity with confidence
Strong team player
Client focused and commercial thinking
Excellent interpersonal and communication skills
Self-motivated and genuine interest in Banking and Finance
Proficiency in Microsoft office (MS Word, Excel & Power point)
